From d5030c4180eeb84a1c0d3df003e879c69dfa3476 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Herwig <contact@michael-herwig.de>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:22:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): an unresolvable OCX_AUTH reference fails the
 mirror run instead of falling back to netrc

ocx_env secret variables now accept file://, env:// and plain:// references,
and SecretVar::get / ReferenceVar::get_slot return Result<_, ReferenceError>;
an unresolvable reference is an error, not an unset variable.

The host-keyed ladder in ocx_mirror_http propagates that error out of resolve,
so the netrc rung and anonymous access are never tried for a host whose
OCX_AUTH_<slug>_{USER,TOKEN} the operator configured. It maps to
MirrorError::AuthReference and keeps the reference error's own exit code.

ocx_oci::auth::Auth::get_or_fallback is fallible for the same reason; the
registry source/destination client builders and ensure_source_auth return
the error as MirrorError::RegistryAuth, classified by ocx's own code.
Presence checks for OCX_ANNOUNCE_TOKEN and CI_JOB_TOKEN use is_set(), which
opens no file.
